<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Aftermission third-party notices</title>
    <style>
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            body {
                background: #333;
                color: white;
            }
            a {
                color: skyblue;
            }
        }
        .container {
            font-family: sans-serif;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }
        .intro {
            text-align: center;
        }
        .licenses-list {
            list-style-type: none;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        .license-used-by {
            margin-top: -10px;
        }
        .license-text {
            max-height: 200px;
            overflow-y: scroll;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <main class="container">
        <div class="intro">
            <h1>Third-party notices</h1>
            <p>The Aftermission web bundle links the open-source components below, each under its own license. Their copyright notices and license texts follow.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Licenses</h2>
        <ul class="licenses-overview">
            {{#each overview}}
            <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>

        <h2>Components and license texts</h2>
        <ul class="licenses-list">
            {{#each licenses}}
            <li class="license">
                <h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
                <h4>Used by:</h4>
                <ul class="license-used-by">
                    {{#each used_by}}
                    <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
                    {{/each}}
                </ul>
                <pre class="license-text">{{text}}</pre>
            </li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>

        <h2>Fonts served with the bundle</h2>
        <p>These are not linked into the bundle: the viewer fetches one when a
            name needs a script the bundled faces do not draw, and a reader who
            opens none never receives them. Each is cut from a Noto original to
            the repertoires DICOM can carry, and each is under the
            <a href="#OFL-1.1">SIL Open Font License 1.1</a> above, with its own
            copyright and a copy of the license in its name table.</p>
        <ul class="licenses-list">
            <li>Noto Sans Hebrew 3.001, Copyright 2024 The Noto Project Authors
                (<a href="https://github.com/notofonts/hebrew">github.com/notofonts/hebrew</a>)</li>
            <li>Noto Sans Arabic 2.013, Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors
                (<a href="https://github.com/notofonts/arabic">github.com/notofonts/arabic</a>)</li>
            <li>Noto Sans Thai 2.002, Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors
                (<a href="https://github.com/notofonts/thai">github.com/notofonts/thai</a>)</li>
            <li>Noto Sans CJK JP 2.004 and Noto Sans CJK KR 2.004, Copyright
                2014-2021 Adobe (<a href="https://www.adobe.com/">adobe.com</a>)</li>
        </ul>
    </main>
</body>

</html>
